ANTI-GROUPTHINK (orchestrator-enforced; you apply them)
- Choose a governing idea and steal elements; never average. Never average two ideas into a third that nobody proposed.
- The lone vision with the highest Dramatic Fidelity is preserved as Option B even if its total is lower.
{% if lone_high_fidelity_lens is defined and lone_high_fidelity_lens %}
  → Round-1 scoring names {{ lone_high_fidelity_lens }} as that lone vision: its governing idea MUST be Option B (unless it is already Option A).
{% endif %}
- A pleasure beat proposed by a single lens that scores Engagement ≥ 8 is carried into Option A or B —
  energy is not allowed to die in committee.
{% if lone_high_engagement is defined and lone_high_engagement %}
  → carry this lone high-engagement pleasure beat from {{ lone_high_engagement.lens }}: "{{ lone_high_engagement.pleasure_offer }}".
{% endif %}
- A device appearing in > 60% of visions is a "consensus device": its Earned Freshness is scored −2 (set consensus_device_penalty on the option that uses it).
{% if consensus_devices is defined and consensus_devices %}
  → consensus devices in this round: {{ consensus_devices | join("; ") }}.
{% endif %}

RULES
- Choose a governing idea. Then steal the best elements from any lens that serve it. Attribute every
  stolen element (contributions[{element, lens}]). Never average two ideas into a third that nobody proposed.
- Every shot carries beat_ref, size, angle, height, lens_mm, movement + motivation, duration, light,
  sound, transitions. Coverage must be shootable within max_setups (estimated_setups × 1.25); if not,
  score Feasibility ≤ 4 and add a reduced_coverage_variant.
- Name the pleasure_beat — what the audience enjoys here. "None" is allowed only for connective scenes and
  must be justified against the pleasure map (pleasure_none_reason). For set-pieces, name the trailer_shot and how
  must_remember lands (must_remember_delivery).
- Energy check: ASL target, camera velocity and cut rate must match the sequence energy_target; an inert
  solution in a high-energy slot scores Engagement ≤ 4, and a frantic solution in a low-energy slot the same.
- Devices: carry devices_used from the chosen option with setup refs; check each against device_permissions
  and the cap ledger. Over-cap → replace or raise HUMAN_QUESTION; never spend a cap silently.
- Write the DIRECTOR'S NOTE: one plain paragraph the human would say to the actors — no camera talk.
- Write the_shot_it_cannot_live_without (a shot_no from the recommended option) and say why.
- Hand each department a one-line stance (colour, music, sound, design, performance) derived from the
  governing idea — each stance says what it ADDS, not only what it avoids; departments elaborate, not re-decide.
- Score A and B with the Resonance Rubric, one-line justification per criterion (justifications[{criterion, note}]).
- List unresolved_tensions honestly. Raise HUMAN_QUESTIONS with two concrete options each and name the conservative one.
- Do not impersonate any lens; attribute, never quote.

